<title>ROMANIA: ROMANIA LISTED CARBID-FOX HAD 1996 HIGHER PROFIT.</title>
<headline>ROMANIA LISTED CARBID-FOX HAD 1996 HIGHER PROFIT.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>					  (billion of leu unless stated)</p>
<p> Gross profit			     7.95     vs     7.40</p>
<p> Net profit				 6.83     vs     4.81</p>
<p> Turnover				 122.65     vs    79.10</p>
<p> Fixed assets			    26.12     vs    24.54</p>
<p> Working capital			 35.83     vs    30.30</p>
<p> Total assets			    62.48     vs    55.34</p>
<p> Share capital			   23.54     vs    23.54</p>
<p> Total debts			     32.22     vs    29.91</p>
<p> Total dividends			  4.01     vs    n.a.</p>
<p> Dividend per share - net	   153.31 lei vs  140.96 lei</p>
<p>NOTE -- Carbid-Fox, Romania's sole carbide producer, is a private company listed on the Bucharest stock exchange's second tier. Data, reported to the bourse, are in nominal terms and in line with Romanian accounting standards. ($=7,089 lei)</p>
<p>-- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
